ly able  to recover from her addiction  except during her boss fight she says  something quite different  you think i wanted this he plied me with  drugs he threatened me  i was 17 i was just a child  he kept her addiction going and she was  a child  it's quite heartbreaking to say the  least if you're noticing a trend  then you're correct joseph preyed upon  impressionable people  including his own family also that he  could further his cause  he's very manipulative and it almost  makes you feel bad for his family  with all this info being shown it's  clear that joseph is the most cruel out  of the three we've discussed  he may not be as well liked as the  previous villains but he is definitely a  very well written one at that  from his crazy motivations and actions  to that energy and power that he emits  that continues to linger in his  followers  submitting to him in doing what he wants  simply by asking so i think it's been  long enough  so let me explain why the definition is  there at the beginning of the video  each game symbolizes this word you can  also think of this word as a phrase  we won but at what cost and this is  arguably the single most defining phrase  of far cry  in each of the far cry games we win but  lose something in the process  jason brody was a simple american kid at  the beginning of the game  not knowing what to do in life but as we  progress we see him change and talking  about how he finally found what he wants  to do in his life and that it actually  has purpose  this all culminates at the final  decision each decision comes at a loss  of something  if jason allies with citra he has to  kill his friends to be a true rocky odd  warrior only to be killed immediately  after by citra herself as she says jason  was born a warrior and he will die a  warrior that's the final part of her  ritual being killed which would explain  why vos thinks citra  is crazy even if hypothetically he would  have lived that stab wound jason would  just live 