ther they deserved it or  not  for the deputy some could argue that we  didn't even win  all the hard work of killing the seed  family and bringing back peace to the  county is all for nothing as the  collapse still happens  all the people we save the quests we did  the vehicles and weapons we all bought  it was a waste of time  joseph was right and he said in the  intro sometimes the best thing to do  is nothing the family needed to be  stopped they killed innocents who didn't  join them and tortured people in the  name of god but it's because  of these actions that caused us to deem  joseph as insane when he was correct the  entire time and lots of people died for  it although depending on your ending you  do get to live the collapse from what i  heard about far cry new dawn the deputy  ends up actually getting brainwashed by  the father since the only thing they  could do in the bunker was think the  deputy was constantly thinking about his  actions whether they were the right  choice or not he would eventually listen  to joseph's word and become part of his  new family  now he's the silent protector of new  eden possibly known as the judge which  is quite a sad turn of events for the  deputy in each of the games we win  we kill or stop the bad guys but each  ending came at the cost of something  relating to our protagonist whether it's  their friends  or their sanity this may be an  over-analysis of the character but the  deputy at the end of the game  is like us when we finish a far cry game  thinking for hours or  days even did we make the right choice  should i have chosen ceball over amida  in my playthrough should jason have  killed his friends  it's never been about choosing the good  or bad option in far cry it's always  been about choosing the lesser of two  evils as even though you may not know  what's coming like with far cry 5  it's a far cry game these aren't happy  fairy tales they're just games that make  us feel powerless yet invigorated in the  b